---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout page={pages.terms}>
  <h2>Using the tools</h2>
  <p>
    Data Formatter Pro provides developer utilities for general information and
    development assistance. You are responsible for the data you process and for
    checking that the result is appropriate for your application. Do not use the
    site to violate applicable law, another person’s rights, or the security of
    systems you are not authorized to access.
  </p>
  <h2>Your data and output</h2>
  <p>
    You retain your rights in your input and output. Local processing does not
    grant the website a license to your payloads. Only process information that
    you are authorized to handle, using a browser and device you trust. These
    tools are not a substitute for a controlled production data-processing
    environment.
  </p>
  <h2>Accuracy and availability</h2>
  <p>
    The tools have documented limits and may contain errors. Verify critical
    results independently before using them in production, security, financial,
    or other consequential decisions. Availability and compatibility can change,
    and no continuous-service commitment is offered.
  </p>
  <h2>Specific technical limitations</h2>
  <p>
    JWT decoding does not authenticate a signature. JavaScript numeric precision
    can affect JSON numbers. CSV conversions can lose type information. Cron
    behavior must be checked against your scheduler. Regex execution is bounded
    but patterns may still be inefficient. See each utility’s guide for its
    detailed behavior.
  </p>
  <h2>Third-party references</h2>
  <p>
    Documentation links are provided for context. Their content, availability,
    and privacy practices are controlled by the relevant third parties. Their
    inclusion does not imply endorsement or affiliation.
  </p>
  <h2>Responsibility and updates</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent allowed by applicable law, the utilities are provided as
    available without warranties of fitness for a particular purpose. Nothing in
    these terms excludes rights or liabilities that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    The operator may revise these terms; the displayed update date identifies
    the version. Contact details and any jurisdiction-specific terms should be
    confirmed before public launch.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>,{' '}
    <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>, and{' '}
    <a href="/contact">contact information</a>.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
